    details = <
        ["de"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::de]>
            purpose = <"Zur Aufzeichnung der bei der körperlichen Untersuchung eines einzelnen Muskels oder einer Muskelgruppe beobachteten Befunde.">
            use = <"Zur Erfassung der beobachteten Befunde bei der körperlichen Untersuchung eines einzelnen Muskels oder einer Muskelgruppe.

Dieser Archetyp wurde speziell für den SLOT „Untersuchungsdetails“ innerhalb der Archetypen OBSERVATION.exam, CLUSTER.exam-nervous_system oder der Archetypenfamilie CLUSTER.exam-joint entwickelt. Er kann, sofern klinisch sinnvoll, auch innerhalb anderer ENTRY- oder CLUSTER-Archetypen verwendet werden. Weitere Spezialisierungen dieses Archetyps ermöglichen die Erfassung von Untersuchungsbefunden für identifizierte Muskeln oder Muskelgruppen.

Die Interpretation der Befunde, z. B. „Keine Auffälligkeit festgestellt“ oder „Mäßige Entzündung vorhanden“, kann mit dem Datenelement „Klinische Interpretation“ erfasst werden.

Dient als Rahmen, in dem CLUSTER-Archetypen in den SLOT „Untersuchungsbefunde“ eingebettet werden können, um zusätzliche strukturierte Befunde aus körperlichen Untersuchungen zu erfassen.

Der Archetyp CLUSTER.exclusion_exam kann im SLOT „Untersuchung nicht durchgeführt“ verschachtelt werden, um optional explizite Details zur nicht durchgeführten Untersuchung aufzuzeichnen.

Verwenden Sie ihn, um die narrativen Beschreibungen klinischer Befunde in bestehenden oder älteren klinischen Systemen mithilfe des Datenelements „Klinische Beschreibung“ in ein archetypisiertes Format zu integrieren.">
            misuse = <"Nicht zur Aufzeichnung der Krankengeschichte verwenden. Verwenden Sie hierfür die spezifischen Archetypen „OBSERVATION“ und „CLUSTER“. Zum Beispiel „OBSERVATION.story“ und „CLUSTER.symptom_sign“.

Nicht zur Aufzeichnung der Ergebnisse einer bildgebenden Untersuchung verwenden. Verwenden Sie hierfür die Archetypenfamilie „CLUSTER.imaging_exam“.">
        >
        ["sv"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::sv]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group. (en)">
            keywords = <"fynd, undersökningsfynd, fysisk undersökning, u.a., utan anmärkning", ...>
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam or the CLUSTER.exam-nervous_system archetypes, or the CLUSTER.exam-joint family of archetypes.It can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. Further specialisations of this archetype can be used to record examination findings for identified muscles or muscle groups.

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"*Not to be used for recording the clinical history - use specific OBSERVATION and CLUSTER archetypes. For example OBSERVATION.story and CLUSTER.symptom_sign.

Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose. (en)">
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group. (en)">
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam or the CLUSTER.exam-nervous_system archetypes, or the CLUSTER.exam-joint family of archetypes.It can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. Further specialisations of this archetype can be used to record examination findings for identified muscles or muscle groups.

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"Skal ikke brukes til å ta opp anamnese - bruk da spesifikke OBSERVATION og CLUSTER arketyper. For eksempel OBSERVATION.story og CLUSTER.symptom_sign.

Skal ikke brukes for å registrere funn ved bildeundersøkelse - bruk arketype innen gruppen av CLUSTER.imaging_exam (Bildeundersøkelse) for dette.">
        >
        ["pt-br"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::pt-br]>
            purpose = <"*To record the findings observed during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group. (en)">
            use = <"*Use to record the observed findings during the physical examination of a single muscle or a muscle group.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the OBSERVATION.exam or the CLUSTER.exam-nervous_system archetypes, or the CLUSTER.exam-joint family of archetypes.It can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate. Further specialisations of this archetype can be used to record examination findings for identified muscles or muscle groups.

Interpretation of the findings, for example 'No abnormality detected' or 'Moderate inflammation present', can be recorded using the 'Clinical interpretation' data element.

Use to provide a framework in which CLUSTER archetypes can be nested in the 'Examination findings' SLOT to record additional structured physical examination findings.

The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.

Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element. (en)">
            misuse = <"*Not to be used for recording the clinical history - use specific OBSERVATION and CLUSTER archetypes. For example OBSERVATION.story and CLUSTER.symptom_sign.

Not to be used for recording the results of an imaging examination - use the CLUSTER.imaging_exam family of archetypes for this purpose. (en)">
